---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import NewsletterForm from '@/components/NewsletterForm.astro';
import { siteConfig, authors } from '@/data/site.config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us"
  description="Meet Nick and Xavier—a home cook and a professional chef who believe great food should work in any kitchen."
>
  <article class="py-12">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-cream-100 to-cream-50 py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="container-narrow text-center">
        <h1 class="text-bark-900 mb-6">Our Story</h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-bark-600">
          What happens when a self-taught home cook and a professionally trained chef
          become friends? You get recipes that actually work.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The Story -->
    <section class="py-12">
      <div class="container-narrow prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        <p>
          We met through mutual friends at a dinner party where Xavier (the chef) spent
          three hours making a sauce that Nick (the home cook) asked if he could "just
          use jarred." The resulting debate lasted longer than the meal.
        </p>

        <p>
          That argument became a friendship, and eventually, this site. We realized
          that most food content falls into two camps: professional recipes that require
          equipment and techniques nobody has at home, or "quick and easy" recipes that
          sacrifice flavor for convenience.
        </p>

        <p>
          We wanted something different: recipes tested from both perspectives, so you
          can decide what's worth the extra effort and what's not.
        </p>

        <h2>What We Do</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Tested Recipes:</strong> Every recipe is made in both a professional
            kitchen and a normal home kitchen. We note what works, what doesn't, and
            what shortcuts are actually worth taking.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Chef vs. Home Cook Features:</strong> We take the same dish and
            cook it two ways—Xavier's way with professional techniques, and Nick's way
            with whatever's in a normal kitchen. Then we tell you when each approach
            makes sense.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Restaurant Reviews:</strong> Honest takes on restaurants in Chicago
            and Houston. We pay for our own meals (usually), and we tell you when we
            don't.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Our Philosophy</h2>

        <p>
          We believe cooking should be enjoyable, not stressful. Sometimes that means
          taking shortcuts. Sometimes that means spending an afternoon perfecting a
          technique. The key is knowing which approach serves the dish—and your life—best.
        </p>

        <p>
          We also believe in transparency. When a meal was comped, we say so. When a
          recipe is sponsored, we say so. Our opinions are always our own.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Meet the Team -->
    <section class="py-12 bg-cream-100">
      <div class="container-wide">
        <h2 class="text-bark-900 text-center mb-12">Meet the Team</h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <!-- Nick -->
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-cozy">
            <img
              src={authors.nick.avatar}
              alt={authors.nick.name}
              class="w-32 h-32 rounded-full mx-auto mb-6 object-cover"
            />
            <h3 class="font-display text-display-md text-bark-900 text-center mb-2">
              {authors.nick.name}
            </h3>
            <p class="text-copper-600 text-center mb-4">{authors.nick.role}</p>
            <p class="text-bark-600 text-center mb-4">{authors.nick.location}</p>
            <p class="text-bark-700 mb-4">{authors.nick.bio}</p>
            <ul class="space-y-1 mb-4">
              {authors.nick.credentials.map((cred) => (
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-bark-600 text-sm">
                  <span class="text-moss-500">✓</span>
                  {cred}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
            <a href="/authors/nick" class="btn-outline w-full text-center">
              See Nick's Work
            </a>
          </div>

          <!-- Xavier -->
          <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-8 shadow-cozy">
            <img
              src={authors.xavier.avatar}
              alt={authors.xavier.name}
              class="w-32 h-32 rounded-full mx-auto mb-6 object-cover"
            />
            <h3 class="font-display text-display-md text-bark-900 text-center mb-2">
              {authors.xavier.name}
            </h3>
            <p class="text-copper-600 text-center mb-4">{authors.xavier.role}</p>
            <p class="text-bark-600 text-center mb-4">{authors.xavier.location}</p>
            <p class="text-bark-700 mb-4">{authors.xavier.bio}</p>
            <ul class="space-y-1 mb-4">
              {authors.xavier.credentials.map((cred) => (
                <li class="flex items-center gap-2 text-bark-600 text-sm">
                  <span class="text-moss-500">✓</span>
                  {cred}
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
            <a href="/authors/xavier" class="btn-outline w-full text-center">
              See Xavier's Work
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Newsletter -->
    <section class="py-12">
      <div class="container-narrow text-center">
        <h2 class="text-bark-900 mb-4">Join Us in the Kitchen</h2>
        <p class="text-bark-600 mb-6">
          Get weekly recipes, restaurant picks, and the occasional friendly debate.
        </p>
        <NewsletterForm showLeadMagnet={true} source="about" />
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
